+
+## Deployment-only trusted origin fork
+
+This local fork preserves the native DNS-rebinding guard by default. Only MCP,
+hooks and plugins management wrappers can additionally accept the exact HTTPS
+origin configured in `SKILLSHARE_UI_TRUSTED_ORIGIN`, received from the actual TCP
+peer in `SKILLSHARE_UI_TRUSTED_PROXY`. The trusted proxy must preserve the browser
+Host, assert HTTPS, and reject other Hosts. Requests still require exact Origin
+or same-origin Fetch Metadata; cross-site, same-site-only, mismatched Origin,
+wrong authority/port, and untrusted peers are denied. Forwarded IP headers never
+establish the trusted peer. This does not add login authentication, change native
+Agent trust, or extend restart/upgrade authorization. Deployment ACLs, artifact
+paths, and rollout evidence belong in deployment documentation.
